964 0 obj
<<
/A 4263 0 R
/Alt (Infographic illustrating the systematic identification of interacting proteins using co-immunoprecipitation or affinity purification, mass spectrometry, and data acquisition, followed by mass data analysis via the ComPASS platform for background removal and identification of real interacting partners of GPX4. The central circle features GPX4 with eight identified interacting proteins including USP71, USP7, Bax, SECISBP2, BAG6, Cdc42, 14-3-3, SLC7A11, HSP70, and VCP. Peripheral panels show the biological functions and pathways involving these interactions, such as cellular energy metabolism, signaling, ferroptosis and cell death, and gene transcription and protein synthesis.)
/K [28 4264 0 R]
/P 244 0 R
/Pg 86 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 4)
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
